  "reported_status": "The campaign reports an end-to-end fixed-exponent Gaussian gradient-mean sampler candidate, an exact dimension-independent baseline Newton–Stein right inverse, and a two-query bounded action for the smoothed Hessian. The full positive Gaussian completion and polylogarithmic query theorem remain unproved. The frozen-source rotation and interface counterexamples refute only their stated constructions. No historic breakthrough is established.",
  "scientific_scope_status": "Model: globally L-Lipschitz conservative g=grad F with F in C^{1,1}, fixed sigma/L>0, whole-vector value access, exact-real Gaussian seeds; target Gaussian mean law in TV epsilon. Reported candidate query count is C_a d^a poly_a(1/epsilon) for each fixed a>0, on every execution; arithmetic/storage are polynomial in the stated model. This does not yield polylogarithmic queries, a finite-bit theorem for the unrounded continuous target, or a full Gaussian noise completion. Two-query Stein action bounds and baseline L2 inverse bounds do not provide one realized symmetric matrix or invert the full operator.",
